import{_ as a,o as t,c as n,ag as s}from"./chunks/framework.BbSdnUwJ.js";const h=JSON.parse('{"title":"Language design","description":"The semantics the RobotDSL language is designed to have, across robot, world, task and evaluation.","frontmatter":{"title":"Language design","description":"The semantics the RobotDSL language is designed to have, across robot, world, task and evaluation."},"headers":[],"relativePath":"development/language.md","filePath":"development/language.md"}'),i={name:"development/language.md"};function r(o,e,d,l,c,p){return t(),n("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[s(`<h1 id="language-design" tabindex="-1">Language design <a class="header-anchor" href="#language-design" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Language design&quot;">​</a></h1><p>This page states the design the language follows. What the compiler accepts today is in the <a href="./../guide/">Guide</a> and the <a href="./../reference/">Reference</a>; where they differ from this page, they describe the current compiler.</p><p>A RobotDSL program combines four descriptions into one checked model.</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Describes</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>CoreDSL</td><td>Components, internal joints, attachment frames, and physical/data interfaces</td></tr><tr><td>WorldDSL</td><td>Scene entities, placement, support surfaces, and task locations</td></tr><tr><td>TaskDSL</td><td>Actions, control flow, inputs, results, and resource use</td></tr><tr><td>EvaluateDSL</td><td>Optional assertions and the observations needed to judge them</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="names-and-values" tabindex="-1">Names and values <a class="header-anchor" href="#names-and-values" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Names and values&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Declarations have explicit names. Imports select declarations from the libraries supplied to the compiler. Missing or ambiguous references are errors; instance names do not imply placement or behavior.</p><p>Physical quantities carry units, and spatial values identify their frames. Static transforms resolve at compile time; dynamic transforms need a runtime provider. An omitted optional argument may use a defined default. An invalid explicit value cannot silently become that default. Missing physical values remain unknown.</p><h2 id="robot-and-world" tabindex="-1">Robot and world <a class="header-anchor" href="#robot-and-world" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Robot and world&quot;">​</a></h2><p>A component can be one rigid body or an articulated subassembly. Instantiation preserves its internal joints and exposes its declared interfaces. Mechanical attachment, power, command, and sensor connections are separate operations. Composition checks their compatibility and the resulting assembly&#39;s constraints.</p><p>World entities carry explicit poses, scale, and static or dynamic behavior. Visual geometry, collision geometry, and navigation maps have separate meanings. A rendered mesh does not establish physical properties or traversability. Named locations and regions provide references for tasks and assertions.</p><h2 id="tasks" tabindex="-1">Tasks <a class="header-anchor" href="#tasks" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Tasks&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Actions declare typed inputs/results, required capabilities, resources, and completion/cancellation behavior. Each action instance has its own arguments.</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Control</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Sequence</td><td>Run children in order, continuing after success</td></tr><tr><td>Fallback</td><td>Try alternatives after failure, stopping at success</td></tr><tr><td>Retry</td><td>Reattempt a failed body within a bound</td></tr><tr><td>Repeat</td><td>Execute a body for a declared number of iterations</td></tr><tr><td>Timeout</td><td>Request cancellation when a deadline expires</td></tr><tr><td>Parallel</td><td>Run children under explicit completion, cancellation, and resource rules</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Pseudocode illustrating branch-specific goals and results:</p><div class="language-text vp-adaptive-theme"><button title="Copy Code" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">text</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark vp-code" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span>sequence:</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>    navigate robot to station_a</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>    image := fallback:</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>        capture camera</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>        sequence:</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>            navigate robot to station_b</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>            capture camera</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>    inspect image</span></span></code></pre></div><p>Both destinations and both branches are checked before execution. Visiting <code>station_b</code> is required only when that branch executes. Every successful path produces the image consumed by <code>inspect</code>.</p><p>A value must be available on every path reaching its use. Failed or cancelled attempts provide no result unless the action declares partial results. Retries have distinct execution identities and cannot reuse stale results accidentally. They do not undo physical effects. Cancellation is a request whose completion must be observed; exclusive resources remain owned until released.</p><h2 id="requirements-and-evaluation" tabindex="-1">Requirements and evaluation <a class="header-anchor" href="#requirements-and-evaluation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Requirements and evaluation&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Provider choices are explicit. Actuation, odometry, state estimation, localization, mapping, planning, and control are separate requirements. Navigation does not universally require lidar or SLAM; the selected provider determines its inputs. Maps, calibration, and pretrained policies are explicit resources. Compilation checks their interfaces and does not perform calibration or training.</p><p>EvaluateDSL checks declare their observations, scope, and timing. Unsupported requested enforcement is an error. Analysis-only requests are identified as such. Missing evidence is not a pass, and user assertions cannot weaken independent benchmark criteria. Physical outcome, execution conformance, and runtime health remain separate results.</p><p>Target-specific restrictions are checked during binding. A target rejects behavior it cannot preserve rather than silently changing the task. See <a href="./architecture.html">Architecture</a> for the compiler boundaries.</p>`,21)])])}const m=a(i,[["render",r]]);export{h as __pageData,m as default};
